12	// This file holds the scripted kubectl the preflight tests run against, and the
13	// preflight tests. The fake is the contract of the kubectl calls the code under
14	// test may issue; the Deploy and Destroy tests reuse it and extend it.
15	//
16	// The Runner receives the arguments WITHOUT "--context <ctx>": injecting it is
17	// the exec runner's job, and the fake fails the test if a call carries one.
18	// "--request-timeout=<d>" may sit anywhere in the arguments; the fake ignores
19	// it, and "--all-namespaces" is read as "-A".
20	//
21	// Calls the fake answers (anything else fails the test as unscripted):
22	//
23	//	config get-contexts -o name
24	//	get --raw /readyz
25	//	auth can-i <verb> <resource> [-n <ns> | -A]
26	//	get namespace <ns> -o json
27	//	get services -A -o json
28	//	get nodes -o json
29	//
30	// "auth can-i" answers like kubectl: "yes" with exit 0, "no" on stdout with exit
31	// 1 (so the Runner returns a non-nil error that is NOT a failure of the call:
32	// the answer is on stdout). "get namespace" of an absent namespace fails with
33	// the kubectl NotFound text on stderr, which means "absent", not an error.
